  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform cable of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is placed on a horizontal surface such that its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> part is hanging below the edge of the surface. To lift the hanging part of the cable upto the surface, the work done should be:"
  },
